{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 72, :comments ["<b>On the eleventh day.</b> I have already explained in the book Moznayim why this number changes, and the meaning of <b>eshtei.</b> Like עשתנותיו — that which his thoughts produce — as though the ten gave birth, and it is a great sod. Rabbi Yonah the Spaniard said that its meaning is \"upon twelve,\" the reason being the count that precedes it. But he erred in two great errors. The first: for the count of twelve is upon eleven, the opposite of his statement, and the trusted witness is from twenty years old and upward. And the second error: for if it were על שתי, it would be fitting to say עשני עשר and not עשתי עשר, for עשתי is feminine, whereas עשני is a single word."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "In the parenthetical gloss of עשתנותיו, the phrase מה שיולידו מחשבותיו is rendered literally as 'that which his thoughts produce,' reflecting a notoriously obscure passage."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:47.352685099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}